   maintainer, who releases them as open content under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, the
   same terms as the bundled Bible text. Built by tools/build_sinksar.py.
   The underlying commemorations are traditional Ethiopian Orthodox
   liturgical content.

   The text is reproduced as the scans carry it, with three disclosed
   exceptions: each paragraph's number is written twice in the source, once
   in Arabic and once in Ge'ez, and only the Ge'ez is kept (all 18,764 of
   them agree, which the generator re-proves on every run); editorial
   dingbats and stray markup are removed; and two Ge'ez days that carry no
   heading block are given one naming their date.

   Earlier releases of Sinq bundled the Amharic synaxarium from the
   gitsaweandsinksarbot project by hailemariam-eyayu
   (https://github.com/hailemariam-eyayu/gitsaweandsinksarbot) and the
   Nexuss0781/synaxarium dataset on the Hugging Face Hub
   (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nexuss0781/synaxarium). Neither is
   bundled any longer.

