CHURCH BOOKS (ሌሎች መጻሕፍት)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The thirty-seven books on the ሌሎች መጻሕፍት shelf — the መልክእ hymns, all of them
scanned out of the printed collection መልክዐ ጉባኤ, together with መጽሐፈ ሰዓታት,
ማኅሌተ ጽጌ, ሰቆቃወ ድንግል and ጸሎት ነቢያት — were scanned from
available PDF scans of the printed books by the Sinq maintainer, and are
released as open content under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0), the same terms as the
bundled scripture. The underlying texts are traditional Ethiopian Orthodox
Tewahedo liturgical material.

The text is reproduced as the scans carry it, with three disclosed exceptions:

  * The printer's tier marks ፪ማ፡ and ማ፡, which mark where a line of a stanza
    breaks, are rendered as those line breaks rather than as characters.
  * መጽሐፈ ሰዓታት is merged from three scanned copies of the printed book the
    Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church publishes on its own site,
    https://www.ethiopianorthodox.org/amharic/holybooks/Metsehafeseatat.pdf.
    The bilingual copy is the spine; the Ge'ez-only copy restores the lines its
    scan dropped; the offices carried only by the ደብረ ዓባይ recension are
    labelled with that name.
  * ጸሎት ነቢያት በአማርኛ has twenty chapters where its scan has fifteen. The five
    it lacked — መኃልየ መኃልይ in the five readings the Ge'ez copy divides it
    into — are the Song of Songs from the bundled Bible (80-weahadu, above),
    not a scan. The Ge'ez copy is missing 2:1–7 at the seam between its first
    two readings; the Amharic is built from a complete text and does not
    reproduce that gap.

  ማኅሌተ ጽጌ is shipped with its Amharic set against the Ge'ez verse by verse.
  ሰቆቃወ ድንግል's Amharic is one verse short of its Ge'ez and nothing in the text
  says which is missing, so it is appended whole under its own heading rather
  than interleaved — a positional pairing would be wrong after the gap.

  Built by tools/build_books.py, tools/merge_seatat.py and tools/merge_tsige.py.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATRISTIC COMMENTARY (CATENA BIBLE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A selected verse offers a link to catenabible.com, where the commentary of the
Church Fathers on that verse is collected. No commentary text is bundled with
the app and nothing is sent when the link is opened: it is an ordinary link,
handed to the browser.

Catena carries 76 books. Sinq carries 93, so seventeen have no page there and
are given no link — the Ethiopian deuterocanon the site does not reach (ሄኖክ,
ኩፋሌ, ፫ መቃብያን, ዕዝራ ካልእ, and the Daniel and Esther fragments) and the nine
broader-canon books. That is 19.5% of the app's verses.

The Psalter's chapter number is translated on the way out. Sinq numbers its
psalms as the Church does, following the Septuagint; Catena numbers them as the
Masoretic text does, so መዝሙር ፳፪ is Psalm 23 there. The table is read out of the
bundled Psalter, whose headings carry the other number in parentheses, and is
held to it by CatenaLinkTest. Every other book is linked unchanged.

